"Back when I was younger\nThick flashy boxes were there\nSeparating reality and fictional hunger\n\nThe boxes slimmed\nLike their fat was dying\nGenerations grinned\nLike cards were vying\n\nBack when I was younger\nVirtual had a definition\nIt was like a joyride\nAfter reality's tribulation\n\nWe had stuff to do\nFrom evening cycling to reading loud\nWe might had a living \"who\"\nWho talked to us like composed\n\nBack when I was younger\nStudy might had an enjoyment\nUnlike the virtuality today\nIt had a moral amusement\n\nIt was not some \"pass in school\"\nIt was not some unreal oneshot\nIt was a development tool\nAnd it demanded whatever we'd got\n\nBack when I was younger\nMorality had some meaning\nEthics were non virtual\nAnd relations were not shredding\n\nWe had dignity and limits\nNot every moron had global connections \nNow that I see the world as it is\nNot every wise have local interactions"